**VERDICT: REJECT**

**Overall Assessment**:
The `BuggyCombobox` component implements approximately 30% of the WAI-ARIA Combobox pattern. While it exposes `role="combobox"`, `aria-autocomplete="list"`, and toggles `aria-expanded`, it completely lacks the underlying semantic popup structure (`role="listbox"`, `role="option"`), has no active-descendant or focus tracking mechanism, fails to connect the combobox to its popup via `aria-controls`, and fails to communicate the number of filtered results or selection changes to assistive technologies. For screen reader users, this functions as an ordinary text input that claims to have an expanded popup that is completely invisible and unreachable in the accessibility tree.

---

### Pre-commitment Predictions
- **Predicted**: Missing `role="listbox"` on the popup and `role="option"` on list items.
- **Predicted**: Missing `aria-controls` referencing the popup container ID on the combobox input.
- **Predicted**: Missing `aria-activedescendant` communication linking the focused input to the active option.
- **Predicted**: Visual selection state (`className="suggestion-item selected"`) not mapped to `aria-selected="true"`.
- **Predicted**: Lack of status announcements (`aria-live`) for number of filtered results.
- **Actual**: All predicted gaps are confirmed present in the component code.

---

### Critical Findings (blocks access)

1. **Popup container lacks `role="listbox"` and options lack `role="option"` / `aria-selected`**
   - **Location**: `BuggyCombobox.jsx:68-80`
   - **Element**: `<div className="suggestions-list">` and child `<div className="suggestion-item">`
   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users (VoiceOver, NVDA, JAWS)
   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value); WAI-ARIA Combobox Pattern & Listbox Pattern
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: A `role="combobox"` contract requires its popup to have a valid role (typically `listbox`, `grid`, `tree`, or `dialog`). Plain `<div>` elements convey no role, meaning screen readers do not recognize the popup as a selectable list of options. When navigating items, screen readers will remain completely silent about option roles, item position (e.g., "1 of 5"), and selection state.
   - **Fix**: Add `role="listbox"` and an accessible name (`aria-label={label}` or `aria-labelledby="combobox-input"`) to the popup container `#suggestions-popup`. Add `role="option"`, unique IDs (e.g., `id={`option-${idx}`}`), and `aria-selected={selectedIndex === idx}` to each item.

2. **Missing `aria-controls` on `<input role="combobox">`**
   - **Location**: `BuggyCombobox.jsx:57-65`
   - **Element**: `<input ... role="combobox" />`
   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users
   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value); WAI-ARIA 1.2 Combobox Specification
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: In ARIA 1.2, `aria-controls` on the combobox input is mandatory when `aria-expanded="true"` to explicitly reference the ID of the popup element (`suggestions-popup`). Without it, assistive tech cannot programmatically determine what element the combobox controls or where to find the popup options.
   - **Fix**: Add `aria-controls={isOpen && filtered.length > 0 ? "suggestions-popup" : undefined}` to the `<input>`.

3. **Missing `aria-activedescendant` synchronization with keyboard navigation**
   - **Location**: `BuggyCombobox.jsx:31-43`, `BuggyCombobox.jsx:57-65`
   - **Element**: `handleKeyDown` and `<input>`
   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users
   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value), WCAG 2.2 SC 2.1.1 (Keyboard); WAI-ARIA APG Combobox with Listbox Popup
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: DOM focus remains trapped in the `<input>` element while arrow keys update only a local component state (`selectedIndex`). Because there is no `aria-activedescendant` property pointing to the ID of the active option, screen reader users receive zero audio feedback when pressing ArrowUp or ArrowDown. Sighted users see a blue/highlighted box, but screen reader users hear nothing.
   - **Fix**: Ensure each option has a stable ID (e.g., `option-${idx}`). Add `aria-activedescendant={selectedIndex >= 0 ? `option-${selectedIndex}` : undefined}` to the `<input>`.

---

### Major Findings (significantly degrades experience)

1. **Mouse / Pointer interactions break focus and don't manage `selectedIndex`**
   - **Location**: `BuggyCombobox.jsx:72-77`
   - **Element**: `<div onClick={() => handleSelect(option)}>`
   - **Impacted Group**: Low-vision / Screen magnifier users, Mouse/Touch users
   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 2.4.3 (Focus Order), WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships)
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: Clicking an item triggers `handleSelect`, but if a user clicks an item, focus may blur off the input depending on browser click defaults. Additionally, hovering over an item does not update `selectedIndex`, creating a desynchronization between hover state and keyboard state.
   - **Fix**: Add `onMouseEnter={() => setSelectedIndex(idx)}` and `onMouseDown={(e) => e.preventDefault()}` on options to prevent the input from losing focus before the `onClick` fires.

2. **No dynamic feedback for filtered result count or empty states**
   - **Location**: `BuggyCombobox.jsx:67-81`
   - **Element**: Render block for suggestions
   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users, Cognitive accessibility users
   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.3 (Status Messages)
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: When the user types "xyz" and 0 options match, the popup simply does not render (`filtered.length > 0`). There is neither an aria-live announcement nor an explicit "No results found" option or status message. Screen reader users cannot tell if results are still loading or if 0 matches were returned.
   - **Fix**: Add an `aria-live="polite"` status container or visually hidden region announcing result count updates (e.g., `"{filtered.length} suggestions available"`).

---

### Minor Findings (friction but workaround exists)

1. **Option selection index handling when opening with ArrowDown**
   - **Location**: `BuggyCombobox.jsx:31-38`
   - **Element**: `handleKeyDown` ArrowDown branch
   - **Impacted Group**: Keyboard-only users
   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WAI-ARIA APG Combobox Pattern
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: When closed, pressing ArrowDown opens the popup, but leaves `selectedIndex` at `-1`. The user must press ArrowDown a second time to highlight the first option, or if the list was already open, it immediately jumps to `0`. Per APG recommendations, opening via ArrowDown should either leave focus on the input or directly select the first option consistently.
   - **Fix**: Standardize whether opening selects the first item (`setSelectedIndex(0)`) or explicitly waits for subsequent keystrokes.

2. **Missing `Tab` key handling to auto-close popup**
   - **Location**: `BuggyCombobox.jsx:31-54`
   - **Element**: `handleKeyDown`
   - **Impacted Group**: Keyboard-only users
   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 2.4.3 (Focus Order)
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: If the user presses `Tab` to leave the combobox while the popup is open, `isOpen` remains `true`. When focus returns, or for layout/visual purposes, the popup remains floating open unless an outside click / onBlur handler is added.
   - **Fix**: Add an `onBlur` listener to close the popup, or close on `Tab` keydown: `if (e.key === 'Tab') setIsOpen(false);`.

---

### What's Missing

- **`role="listbox"` & `role="option"`**: Fundamental missing ARIA roles for popup suggestions.
- **`aria-controls="suggestions-popup"`**: Programmatic link between combobox input and popup element.
- **`aria-activedescendant`**: Binding active item ID to input focus.
- **`aria-selected="true|false"`**: Programmatic indication of option selection.
- **`onBlur` / Outside Click Dismissal**: Focus management when tabbing or clicking outside the widget.
- **Result Count Live Region**: Feedback when filter queries change the result set.

---

### Multi-Perspective Notes & Alarm Levels

| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Screen reader** | **HIGH** | Role combobox without listbox/options/activedescendant | Critical failure. Completely unusable via assistive technology; behaves like an unassisted textbox with silent phantom menus. |
| **Keyboard-only** | **MEDIUM** | Missing Tab/blur dismissal, inconsistent initial index on open | Operable via Arrow keys and Enter, but lacks outside dismissal and robust focus retention. |
| **Low vision** | **MEDIUM** | Visual contrast of selection state, focus containment | Depends on CSS `.selected` styling; needs verification for 3:1 indicator contrast. |
| **Cognitive** | **MEDIUM** | No feedback on 0 results / search filtering | Disappearance of popup with no "No results" message is disorienting. |
| **Vestibular & motion** | **LOW** | No animations or auto-motion | No issues identified. |
| **Auditory access** | **LOW** | No audio elements | Not applicable. |
| **Environmental contrast** | **MEDIUM** | Dependent on CSS styling | Ensure `.suggestion-item.selected` has high-contrast background and text. |

---

### Remediated Implementation Reference

```jsx
import React, { useState, useRef, useId } from 'react';

const AccessibleCombobox = ({ label, options = [] }) => {
  const [input, setInput] = useState('');
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);
  const [selectedIndex, setSelectedIndex] = useState(-1);
  const inputRef = useRef(null);

  const comboboxId = useId();
  const listboxId = `${comboboxId}-listbox`;

  const filtered = input
    ? options.filter((opt) => opt.toLowerCase().includes(input.toLowerCase()))
    : options;

  const handleInputChange = (e) => {
    setInput(e.target.value);
    setIsOpen(true);
    setSelectedIndex(-1);
  };

  const handleSelect = (value) => {
    setInput(value);
    setIsOpen(false);
    setSelectedIndex(-1);
    inputRef.current?.focus();
  };

  const handleKeyDown = (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'ArrowDown') {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (!isOpen) {
        setIsOpen(true);
        setSelectedIndex(filtered.length > 0 ? 0 : -1);
      } else if (filtered.length > 0) {
        setSelectedIndex((prev) => (prev < filtered.length - 1 ? prev + 1 : 0));
      }
    } else if (e.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (!isOpen) {
        setIsOpen(true);
        setSelectedIndex(filtered.length > 0 ? filtered.length - 1 : -1);
      } else if (filtered.length > 0) {
        setSelectedIndex((prev) => (prev > 0 ? prev - 1 : filtered.length - 1));
      }
    } else if (e.key === 'Enter') {
      if (isOpen && selectedIndex >= 0 && selectedIndex < filtered.length) {
        e.preventDefault();
        handleSelect(filtered[selectedIndex]);
      }
    } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {
      if (isOpen) {
        e.preventDefault();
        setIsOpen(false);
        setSelectedIndex(-1);
      }
    } else if (e.key === 'Tab') {
      setIsOpen(false);
      setSelectedIndex(-1);
    }
  };

  const activeDescendantId =
    isOpen && selectedIndex >= 0 ? `${comboboxId}-opt-${selectedIndex}` : undefined;

  return (
    <div className="combobox-wrapper">
      <label htmlFor={comboboxId}>{label}</label>
      <div className="combobox-control">
        <input
          ref={inputRef}
          id={comboboxId}
          type="text"
          value={input}
          onChange={handleInputChange}
          onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
          onBlur={() => {
            // Small timeout to allow option click to register before closing
            setTimeout(() => setIsOpen(false), 150);
          }}
          role="combobox"
          aria-autocomplete="list"
          aria-expanded={isOpen}
          aria-controls={isOpen && filtered.length > 0 ? listboxId : undefined}
          aria-activedescendant={activeDescendantId}
        />
      </div>

      {/* Screen reader status announcement for filtered options */}
      <div className="sr-only" aria-live="polite" role="status">
        {isOpen && `${filtered.length} suggestion${filtered.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} available.`}
      </div>

      {isOpen && filtered.length > 0 && (
        <ul
          role="listbox"
          id={listboxId}
          aria-label={label}
          className="suggestions-list"
        >
          {filtered.map((option, idx) => {
            const isSelected = selectedIndex === idx;
            return (
              <li
                key={option}
                id={`${comboboxId}-opt-${idx}`}
                role="option"
                aria-selected={isSelected}
                onMouseDown={(e) => e.preventDefault()} // Prevents input blur before click fires
                onClick={() => handleSelect(option)}
                className={isSelected ? 'suggestion-item selected' : 'suggestion-item'}
              >
                {option}
              </li>
            );
          })}
        </ul>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default AccessibleCombobox;
```

---

### Verdict Justification
**Verdict: REJECT**
The component claims to be an accessible combobox via `role="combobox"`, but lacks the underlying semantic popup roles (`listbox`, `option`), connection links (`aria-controls`), active option announcements (`aria-activedescendant`), and programmatic selection indicators (`aria-selected`). This renders the widget completely inaccessible to screen reader users, violating WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 and SC 2.1.1. To reach an `ACCEPT` verdict, the full WAI-ARIA 1.2 Combobox pattern must be implemented as demonstrated above.
